  Hummingbird is intended to be released under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  This placeholder records that intent so the repository has an unambiguous
  license from its first commit. Before the first public release, replace this
  file with the full, verbatim Apache-2.0 text (including the appendix and the
  copyright line below) and add SPDX headers to source files:

      SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

  Attribution Notice:
    This project is heavily inspired by Colibri (https://github.com/JustVugg/colibri),
    and shares the Apache-2.0 license to ensure attribution and reuse compatibility.
    While Colibri inspired this project, Hummingbird follows a completely different
    architecture and approach. Colibri focuses on running GLM-5.2 (744B MoE) on a
    25GB-RAM machine, whereas Hummingbird provides a generalized, modular inference
    framework to run any model through its adapter interface.

